+    // that finds none free waits in `waiters` for one of exactly two events:
+    // a release hands it the released helper, or a helper leaves the pool
+    // (exit, failed spawn, failed send, or an error reply, after which it is
+    // killed) and `retire` hands it that helper's slot to fork a successor.
+    // Every way a helper can stop serving goes through `retire`, so no waiter
+    // waits for a slot nothing will free.
+    class TaskOutputLeases {
+        constructor(parallelism, invocationTracker, purpose) {
+            this.purpose = purpose;
+            this.invocationTracker = invocationTracker;
+            this.parallelism = Math.max(1, parallelism);
